    gameId: 'five-hundred',
    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Bidding Phase**: Starting with player left of dealer, each player bids the number of tricks they believe they can win (6-10) and optionally names trump or passes. Bids increase; last bid stands (highest wins). Player may bid only once. 2. **Kitty Discovery**: Winning bidder takes the 3-card kitty, examines it, and discards 3 cards face-down (kitty discards are never revealed). 3. **Trump Declaration**: High bidder announces trump suit OR 'No Trumps' (or 'Misere' / 'Open Misere' if their contract value supports it). 4. **Play Phase**: High bidder leads the first trick. Each player must follow suit if able. Trick won by highest trump or highest card of led suit. Trick winner leads next. 5. **Scoring**: After all 10 tricks, count tricks won by high bidder's partnership. If bid made: partners score the contract points. If failed: partners score negative points; opponents score 10 per trick won. 6. **Next Deal**: Deal passes left after each hand.",
    Player: "1. **Bidding Phase**: Starting with player left of dealer, each player bids the number of tricks they believe they can win (6-10) and optionally names trump or passes. Bids increase; last bid stands (highest wins). Player may bid only once. 2. **Kitty Discovery**: Winning bidder takes the 3-card kitty, examines it, and discards 3 cards face-down (kitty discards are never revealed). 3. **Trump Declaration**: High bidder announces trump suit OR 'No Trumps' (or 'Misere' / 'Open Misere' if their contract value supports it). 4. **Play Phase**: High bidder leads the first trick. Each player must follow suit if able. Trick won by highest trump or highest card of led suit. Trick winner leads next. 5. **Scoring**: After all 10 tricks, count tricks won by high bidder's partnership. If bid made: partners score the contract points. If failed: partners score negative points; opponents score 10 per trick won. 6. **Next Deal**: Deal passes left after each hand.",
    objective: 'First partnership to score 500+ points wins the game. Points are earned by making bid contracts.',
    gameplay: "1. **Bidding Phase**: Starting with player left of dealer, each player bids the number of tricks they believe they can win (6-10) and optionally names trump or passes. Bids increase; last bid stands (highest wins). Player may bid only once. 2. **Kitty Discovery**: Winning bidder takes the 3-card kitty, examines it, and discards 3 cards face-down (kitty discards are never revealed). 3. **Trump Declaration**: High bidder announces trump suit OR 'No Trumps' (or 'Misere' / 'Open Misere' if their contract value supports it). 4. **Play Phase**: High bidder leads the first trick. Each player must follow suit if able. Trick won by highest trump or highest card of led suit. Trick winner leads next. 5. **Scoring**: After all 10 tricks, count tricks won by high bidder's partnership. If bid made: partners score the contract points. If failed: partners score negative points; opponents score 10 per trick won. 6. **Next Deal**: Deal passes left after each hand.",
    keyRules: [
      '**Card Rankings**: In trump suit: Joker (highest) > Right Bower (jack of trump) > Left Bower (jack of same color) > A > K > Q > 10 > 9 > 8 > 7. Non-trump: A > K > Q > J > 10 > 9 > 8 > 7.',
      '**Bowers**: The jack of trump suit (Right Bower) and the jack of the same color as trump (Left Bower) are the two highest-ranking cards in trump.',
      '**No Trumps**: All suits rank normally (A-K-Q-J-10...7). Joker is a nominate card (player specifies which suit it belongs to before play) or unsuit card (playable only when void in led suit).',
      '**Misere**: Contractor must lose all 10 tricks. Partners never score points; only contractors lose (if successful, they score 250 points; if failed, negative points). Joker and bowers irrelevant.',
      "**Open Misere**: Misere with contractor's hand exposed after first trick. Scores 500 points if successful.",
      '**Trick Management**: Must follow suit if able; otherwise, any card may be played. No forced trump.',
      "**Kitty Discard**: High bidder's three discarded cards are never revealed and are not counted in scoring.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Exactly 4 players in 2 fixed partnerships (seated opposite each other).',
      deck: '43-card deck: Remove all 2s, 3s, 4s, 5s, 6s from a standard 52-card deck, keeping 7-A in all suits. Add 1 Joker. Total: 43 cards + 1 Joker = 44 cards.',
      equipment: 'Deck, scoresheet, pencil, dealer button (optional).',
      dealing: 'Dealer shuffles and right-hand player cuts. Dealer distributes: 3 cards to each player, then 3 cards to the kitty (widow), then 4 more cards to each player. Final distribution: each player holds 10 cards; 3-card kitty placed in center.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Bidding Phase**: Starting with player left of dealer, each player bids the number of tricks they believe they can win (6-10) and optionally names trump or passes. Bids increase; last bid stands (highest wins). Player may bid only once. 2. **Kitty Discovery**: Winning bidder takes the 3-card kitty, examines it, and discards 3 cards face-down (kitty discards are never revealed). 3. **Trump Declaration**: High bidder announces trump suit OR 'No Trumps' (or 'Misere' / 'Open Misere' if their contract value supports it). 4. **Play Phase**: High bidder leads the first trick. Each player must follow suit if able. Trick won by highest trump or highest card of led suit. Trick winner leads next. 5. **Scoring**: After all 10 tricks, count tricks won by high bidder's partnership. If bid made: partners score the contract points. If failed: partners score negative points; opponents score 10 per trick won. 6. **Next Deal**: Deal passes left after each hand.",
