      'Setup example: 10 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: First partnership to score 500+ points wins the game. Points are earned by making bid contracts.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Bidding Phase**: Starting with player left of dealer, each player bids the number of tricks they believe they can win (6-10) and optionally names trump or passes. Bids increase; last bid stands (highest wins). Player may bid only once. 2. **Kitty Discovery**: Winning bidder takes the 3-card kitty, examines it, and discards 3 cards face-down (kitty discards are never revealed). 3. **Trump Declaration**: High bidder announces trump suit OR 'No Trumps' (or 'Misere' / 'Open Misere' if their contract value supports it). 4. **Play Phase**: High bidder leads the first trick. Each player must follow suit if able. Trick won by highest trump or highest card of led suit. Trick winner leads next. 5. **Scoring**: After all 10 tricks, count tricks won by high bidder's partnership. If bid made: partners score the contract points. If failed: partners score negative points; opponents score 10 per trick won. 6. **Next Deal**: Deal passes left after each hand.",
      'Scoring example: Scoring based on contract value and tricks won. First partnership to 500+ points wins. First partnership to reach 500 or more cumulative points wins the game..',
